WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
After the move of the capital, Emperor Xiaowen began to push through a whole series of reforms.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.982
He was still young, yet he had very great determination.

00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:16.300
He encouraged the Xianbei people to adopt Han surnames — even the imperial Tuoba clan changed its surname to Yuan.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:21.810
Everyone took off their Xianbei dress and changed into Central Plains clothing, and the streets took on a completely new look.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.504
Walking the streets of Luoyang, everywhere there was a fresh new atmosphere.

00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:33.382
Chinese also became the language everyone had to learn, and the schoolrooms rang with the sound of reading.

00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:38.412
The children studied earnestly, and the adults learned along with them.

00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:47.114
Different peoples celebrated festivals together and lived together, and their cultures slowly blended into one.

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:51.448
Everyone learned from one another, and life grew more harmonious day by day.

00:00:51.798 --> 00:00:57.486
Although some nobles were not very happy, the steps of reform did not stop.

00:00:57.836 --> 00:01:01.220
These reforms deeply influenced the China that came after.

